        "id": "T2-New-05",
        "topic": "Sports Sponsorship & Advertising",
        "question": "Many companies today sponsor sports as a way of advertising themselves. Some people think that this is a good thing for the world of sports. Others think this has disadvantages. Discuss both these views and give your own opinion.",
        "guide": "<strong>Dạng bài:</strong> Discuss both views & give opinion<br><strong>Cấu trúc gợi ý:</strong><br>- Body 1: Lợi ích của tài trợ (Hỗ trợ tài chính, nâng cấp cơ sở vật chất, quảng bá thể thao).<br>- Body 2: Bất lợi (Quảng bá sản phẩm không lành mạnh, thương mại hóa quá mức).<br>- Opinion: Lợi ích vượt trội hơn nếu được kiểm soát chặt chẽ.",
        "vocab": [
          "Corporate sponsorship (Tài trợ từ doanh nghiệp)",
          "Ubiquitous (Có mặt ở khắp nơi)",
          "Ethical compromise (Sự thỏa hiệp về đạo đức)",
          "Substantial capital (Nguồn vốn đáng kể)",
          "Commercialization (Sự thương mại hóa)"
        ],
        "sample": "Corporate sponsorship in sports has become ubiquitous in the modern era. While supporters argue that it injects vital funding into athletic programs, critics highlight the potential ethical compromises involved. In my view, the financial benefits of such sponsorships significantly outweigh the drawbacks, provided that there are strict regulations regarding the types of products advertised.\n\nOn the positive side, corporate sponsorships bring immense financial benefits to the sporting world. Professional sports require substantial capital to build state-of-the-art stadiums, fund youth training academies, and pay athletes' salaries. Without the financial backing of large corporations, many sporting events simply could not take place on a global scale. Furthermore, this influx of money allows for the broadcasting of events to millions of fans worldwide, thereby promoting a culture of fitness and inspiring younger generations to participate in athletic activities.\n\nConversely, there are valid concerns regarding the negative impacts of corporate advertising in sports. The primary disadvantage is the potential promotion of unhealthy products. Many major sporting events are sponsored by fast-food chains, sugary drink brands, or alcohol companies. Broadcasting these brands to a massive audience, particularly children, contradicts the very essence of sports, which is to promote a healthy lifestyle. Additionally, some argue that the excessive commercialization of sports shifts the focus away from athletic excellence and sportsmanship, turning games into mere marketing platforms.\n\nIn conclusion, while the advertising of unhealthy products through sports sponsorships poses a legitimate concern, the financial support provided by corporations is indispensable for the growth and sustainability of the sporting industry. Therefore, as long as authorities impose strict guidelines on which products can be promoted, corporate sponsorship remains a highly beneficial practice for the world of sports.",
